"1400" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="20000"/><a:lumOff val="80000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>is a Technical Leader &amp; Field CTO at IBM, helping clients solve complex business challenges through technology strategy, architecture, and innovation.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0" defTabSz="914400"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="20000"/><a:lumOff val="80000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>Prior to returning to IBM, DJ spent 17 years at MAPSYS, a premier IBM Business Partner based in Columbus, Ohio. As Executive Director &amp; Chief Architect, he led the company’s reseller business for a decade, delivering sustained year-over-year revenue growth and guiding clients through the evolution of enterprise infrastructure.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0" defTabSz="914400"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="20000"/><a:lumOff val="80000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>DJ began his career at IBM as a microprocessor design engineer, developing processor logic for Apple G5 Macs, Nintendo Wii and Wii U consoles, and IBM Power servers before transitioning into technical sales. He holds six patents and has authored several published papers.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0" defTabSz="914400"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1400" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="20000"/><a:lumOff val="80000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>DJ earned a Bachelor of Science in Computer Engineering from Rutgers University and a Master of Science in Electrical Engineering from the University of Vermont. Throughout his career, his passion has remained the same: bringing together exceptional people and technology to solve customer problems.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1" defTabSz="914400"/><a:endParaRPr lang="en-GB" sz="1400" kern="0" dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1" defTabSz="914400"/><a:endParaRPr lang="en-GB" sz="1400" kern="0" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="Picture 3"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{66704CA7-E0A3-C6EE-C035-C7B548E5E51E}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId4"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="7327900" y="201168"/><a:ext cx="1587500" cy="1587500"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr></p:pic><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="14" name="page-number"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="8156448" y="4887087"/><a:ext cx="457200" cy="210312"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" lIns="0" tIns="0" rIns="0" bIns="0" anchor="t"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr algn="r"/><a:r><a:rPr sz="975" b="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="A6B5CE"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Helvetica Neue"/></a:rPr><a:t>52</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree><p:extLst><p:ext uri="{BB962C8B-B14F-4D97-AF65-F5344CB8AC3E}"><p14:creationId xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" val="2651394715"/></p:ext></p:extLst></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>